# --- Backports is opt-in only, never a blanket upgrade ---
#
# Building on stable is the point: we want a small, audited, predictable base.
# Pulling the whole desktop from backports would quietly turn IRN OS into a
# testing spin. So backports defaults to priority -1 (apt will not install from
# it at all) and we raise only what the target GPU actually needs.
#
# NOTE ON THE PIN FIELD: backports' Release file says `Suite: stable-backports`
# but `Codename: trixie-backports`. Pinning with `a=trixie-backports` matches
# NOTHING and fails silently -- the build succeeds and you ship the old kernel
# anyway. Use `n=` (codename). Verified against the live Release file 2026-08-30.
#
# NOTE ON THE GLOB: this MUST be the whole `linux-*` family, not an enumerated
# list of packages. Kernel 7.x splits into far more binary packages than trixie's
# 6.12 did -- linux-image-amd64 pulls linux-base-amd64, which pulls
# linux-base-<ver>-amd64, linux-binary-<ver>-amd64 and linux-modules-<ver>-amd64.
# Naming them one at a time leaves whichever you forgot sitting at priority -1,
# and the build dies mid-install with:
#     linux-image-amd64 : Depends: linux-base-amd64 (= 7.1.8-1~bpo13+1)
#                         but it is not installable
#     E: Unable to correct problems, you have held broken packages.
# (That failure cost a full build run on 2026-08-31. `apt-cache policy` does NOT
# catch it -- policy only resolves a *candidate version*. Verify a pin change with
# `apt-get install -s linux-image-amd64`, which actually solves dependencies.)
#
# Audited with that simulation: 7 of 79 packages come from backports (the six
# linux-* kernel packages plus firmware-amd-graphics). wpasupplicant and the rest
# of the desktop still resolve to stable, which is exactly the intent.

Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie-backports
Pin-Priority: -1

# The whole kernel family, plus all firmware in lockstep (they share the one
# `firmware-nonfree` source, so mixing a backports firmware-amd-graphics with
# stable siblings gives an unsatisfiable version skew at install time).
Package: linux-* firmware-*
Pin: release n=trixie-backports
Pin-Priority: 600
